              "x": "Let me be honest with you the way most programs won't: there's nothing magical about 10,000. It's just the general number everyone landed on, and it works. For most people it burns an extra 300 to 500 calories a day, it requires zero athletic ability, it doesn't leave you sore, and it doesn't make you hate your life the way forced running does. You can run if you love it. You never have to."
